usb: gadget: f_mass_storage: keep the idle count across sleep_thread calls

sleep_thread() only checks for eject/Ctrl-C after 200000 idle loop
iterations, and the counters were local, so every host command reset
them. A host polling removable media every couple of seconds meant an
eject was never noticed and ums never returned. Make the counters static.

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c	2026-10-25 13:49:26.934521932 -0400
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c	2026-10-25 13:49:26.961798880 -0400
@@ -650,7 +650,12 @@
 static int sleep_thread(struct fsg_common *common)
 {
 	int	rc = 0;
-	int i = 0, k = 0;
+	/*
+	 * Keep the idle count across calls. Hosts poll removable media every
+	 * few seconds (TEST UNIT READY), which used to reset the count before
+	 * it reached the eject/Ctrl-C check, so an eject was never acted on.
+	 */
+	static int i, k;
 
 	/* Wait until a signal arrives or we are woken up */
 	for (;;) {
